Playwright Automation Framework

1. Project Overview

    This automation testing framework is developed with Playwright with typescript

    The framework is designed to support both web application and API automation testing. it follows page object model, resuable custom fixtures and seperate test data management.

    The primary objective to improve code resuability, maintainability, scalability and test execution efficiency.

2. Technology Stack

    1. Playwright
    2. TypeScript
    3. Node.js
    4. Page Object Model (POM)
    5. Custom Playwright Fixtures
    6. JSON-based Test Data
    7. Playwright API Testing
    8. Allure Reporting

3. Framework Architecture:

    This framework organized into following layers

    1. Configuration Layer
        *playwright.config.ts => Manages playwright test execution configuration
        *tsconfig.json => Typescript compiler configuration
        *package.json = > Project dependencies and execution scripts
    2. Page Object Layer
        Located under src/pages/.
            *BagePage.ts => Common reusable page interaction methods
            *LoginPage.ts => contains locator and actions of login page
            *CartPage.ts => contains locators and actions of Cartpage.ts
            *InventoryPage.ts => contains locators and actions of InventoryPage.ts
    3. Fixture Layer
        Located under src/fixtures
            *pagefixture.ts => provides resuable custom fixtures and page object initialization.
    4. TestData Layer
        Located under src/testData/.
        Stores test data seperately from test implementation
        Supports data driven test execution
            *loginpageData.json => test data that used in loginpage
            *checkoutpageData.json => test data that used in checkout page
    5. Utilities Layer
        Located under src/utilities/.
        contains reusable helper functions and common utilites like json file reader.(future enhancement)
    6. Test Layer
        Located under tests/.
        Page wise tests with the scenarios and its scripts using custom page fixtures and functions from respective page files.
    7. Reporting Layer
        Located under allure-report/. => Stores test reporting output
        Located under allure-results/. => Stores test execution artifacts
    
4. Design Pattern

    The framework follows page object model design pattern

    Each application page is represented by an individual typescript classes. Each has its locators and actions are encapsulated within the classes.

    Common methods are maintained in the BasePage class to avoid code duplication.
    
    Custom Playwright fixtures are used to initialize and provide page objects to test scripts.

5. UI Test Execution Flow

    1. Execute playwright command
    2. Playwright loads the configuration file
    3. Test runner identifies the matching test specifications.
    4. Custom fixtures initialize the required page objects.
    5. Test data retrieved from the relevant data file
    6. Page object methods perform browser interactions
    7. Assertions validates the expected results.
    8. Test execution results and reports are generated.

6. Reporting

    Reporting helps to analayze test results

    Allure reports are used in this framework as its provides detailed test reports, screenshots, videos, traces, categories and historical trends.

7. Key Framework Benefits

    1. Layered Automation framework
    2. Seperation of test logic and page-specific implementation
    3. Reusable page objects
    4. Centralized common page interactions
    5. Custom fixture based page object initialization
    6. Seperation of test data and automation logic
    7. Support UI and API validation
    8. Maintainable and scalable framework

8. Future Enhancements

    1. CI/CD pipeline integration.
    2. Cross-browser execution.
    3. Parallel execution optimization.
    4. Enhanced API test coverage.
    5. Improved reporting and execution analytics including Emailing and sending reports via teams.
    6. PDF validations
    7. Environment-specific configuration management.
